1	TSA	Tryptic Soy Agar	Tryptic Soy Agar powder 40 g (pancreatic digest of casein 15 g, papaic digest of soybean 5 g, NaCl 5 g, agar 15 g), distilled water 1 liter, heat the mixture while stirring to fully dissolve all components. Autoclave at 121 °C for 15 minutes.
2	NA	Nutrient Agar	Nutrient agar powder 28 g (lab-lemco powder 1 g, yeast extract 2 g, peptone 5 g, NaCl 5 g, agar 15g), distilled water 1 liter, heat the mixture while stirring to fully dissolve all components. Autoclave at 121 °C for 15 minutes.
3	TSB	Tryptic Soy Broth	Tryptic Soy Broth powder 30 g (casein peptone 17 g, soy peptone 3 g, NaCl 5 g, K2HPO4 2,5 g, glucose 2,5 g), distilled water 1 liter, heat the mixture while stirring to fully dissolve all components. Autoclave at 121 °C for 15 minutes.
4	NB	Nutrient Broth	Nutrient broth powder 13 g (lab-lemco 1 g, yeast extract 2 g, peptone 5 g, NaCl 5g), distilled water 1 liter, heat the mixture while stirring to fully dissolve all components. Autoclave at 121 °C for 15 minutes.
6	TBT	Trypan blue and Tetracycline	20 g agar, 2 g glucose, 1 g L-asparagine, 1 g NaHCO3, 500 mg KH2PO4, 100 MG MgSO4 · 7H2O, 50 mg trypan blue (TB). pH adjusted to 5.5 with 10% phosphoric acid (4ml/liter). Autoclave the dissolved mixture at 121 °C for 15 minutes. Add filter-sterilized (pore size, 0.22 μm) tetracycline (20 g Tetracycline) to the autoclaved medium.
7	PCAT	Pseudomonas cepacia azelaic acid tryptamine) medium	MgSO4, 0.1 g, azelaic acid 2 g, tryptamine 0.2 g; K2 HPO4 4 g, KH2 PO4 4 g, yeast extract 0.02 g, agar, 15 g, pH adjusted to 5.7. Autoclave the dissolved mixture at 121 °C for 15 minutes. Add filter-sterilized (pore size, 0.22 μm) cycloheximide (200 mgl-1) and crystal violet 2 mgl-1) to the autoclaved medium.
8	BAc	?????	2 g azelaic acid, 0,4 g K2HPO4, 0,4 g KH2PO4, 0,2 g MgSO4 · 7H2O, 0,075 g Bromothymol blue, 0,2 g L-citrulline. Distilled water 1 liter. pH adjusted at 5,7. Autoclave at 121°C 20 min. After sterilization, add filter-sterilized (pore size, 0.22 μm) citrulline.
9	BAz	Nitrogen-free semisolid medium	2 g azelaic acid, 0,4 g K2HPO4, 0,4 g KH2PO4, 0,2 g MgSO4 · 7H2O, 0,02 g CaCl2, 0,002 g Na2MoO4 · H2O, 0,01 g FeCl3, 0,075 g Bromothymol blue, 2,3 g agar. Distilled water 1 liter. pH adjusted to 5.7 with KOH. Vials containing 5ml of BAz medium are autoclaved at 121°C for 20 min.
10	TN	Modified version of ATCC 197 medium	NaCl, 10.0 g, KCl 0.1 g, MgCl2 6H2O 0.2g, NH4Cl 1,0 g, KH2PO4 0.3 g, CaCl2· 2H2O 0.1 g, cysteine-HCl 1.0 g, yeast extract 2.0 g, tryptone 2.0 g, glucose 5.0 g, resazurin(redox indicator) 0.001 g. Distilled water 1 liter. Before sterilization, adjust pH at 7.0with 1 M NaOH . Autoclave at 121°C 20 min. After sterilization, add 10 ml of water sterilized vitamins and trace element solution from DSM medium 141.
11	PDA	Potato dextrose agar	Potato Dextrose Agar powder (Dextrose 20 g/L, Potato extract 4 g/L, Agar 15 g/L) 41 g, distilled water 1 liter, heat the mixture while stirring to fully dissolve all components. Autoclave at 121 °C for 20 minutes.Add filter-sterilized (pore size, 0.22 μm) streptomycin (300 mgl-1) and neomycin (150 mgl-1) to the autoclaved medium.
12	MEA	Malt Extract Agar	agar, 15 g/L, malt extract, 30 g/L, mycological peptone, 5 g/L
13	HM372	Halobacteria Medium	Yeast extract 5.00 g; Casamino acids 5.00 g; Na glutamate 1.00 g; KCl 2.00\tg; Na3-citrate 3.00 g; MgSO4x7H2O 20.00 g; NaCl 200.00\tg; FeCl2x4H2O 36.00 mg\t; MnCl2x4H2O 0.36 mg; Agar 20.00 g; Distilled water\t 1000\tml
14	YPD	Yeast Peptone Destrose Agar	Agar 15 g/L, Bacteriological peptone 20 g/L, Glucose 20 g/L, Yeast extract 10 g/L
15	GYM	Glucose yeast extract medium	Glucose 20 g/L, Yeast extract 10 g/L, CaCO3 (light precipitate) 20g/L, Agar 17 g/L
16	BG-11	Freshwater medium	https://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/12/14/2806
17	Mann and Myers medium	Mann and Myers medium	NaNO3 (1.0 g/L), K2HPO4 (0.1 g/L), MgSO4·7H2O (1.2 g/L), and CaCl2 (0.3 g/L). Also, a micronutrient solution of 10 mL was added into 990 mL of Mann and Myers medium. The micronutrients stock solution contained Na2EDTA (0.001 mg/L), MnCl2 (1.4 mg/L), ZnSO4·7H2O (0.33 mg/L), FeSO4·2H2O (2 mg/L), CuSO4·5H2O (0.002 mg/L), and Co(NO3)2·6H2O (0.007 mg/L).
