5	TBT	Trypan blue and Tetracycline	20 g agar, 2 g glucose, 1 g L-asparagine, 1 g NaHCO3, 500 mg KH2PO4, 100 MG MgSO4 · 7H2O, 50 mg trypan blue (TB). pH adjusted to 5.5 with 10% phosphoric acid (4ml/liter). Autoclave the dissolved mixture at 121 °C for 15 minutes. Add filter-sterilized (pore size, 0.22 μm) tetracycline (20 g Tetracycline) to the autoclaved medium.	1
6	PCAT	Pseudomonas cepacia azelaic acid tryptamine) medium	MgSO4, 0.1 g, azelaic acid 2 g, tryptamine 0.2 g; K2 HPO4 4 g, KH2 PO4 4 g, yeast extract 0.02 g, agar, 15 g, pH adjusted to 5.7. Autoclave the dissolved mixture at 121 °C for 15 minutes. Add filter-sterilized (pore size, 0.22 μm) cycloheximide (200 mgl-1) and crystal violet 2 mgl-1) to the autoclaved medium.	1
