0	AE	AE medium (Gluconobacter medium)	Glucose 15.00 g/L, Peptone 3.00 g/L, Yeast extract 2.00 g/L, Acetic acid 65.00 mL/L, Ethanol 20.00 mL/L, Agar 9.00 g/L. Add solid components to distilled/deionized water without the addition of glacial acetic acid and absolute ethanol. Sterilize by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 minutes. Add glacial acetic acid and absolute ethanol after sterilization either by filtration (use Teflon filters).
1	MA	Milk agar	Sodium citrate 20.00 g/L, Skimmed milk powder 10.00 g/L, Agar 8.00 g/L. Dissolve the sodium citrate to distilled/deionized water and adjust the pH to 7.5. Add the agar. pH 7.5 ± 0.2 at 25°C. Sterilize by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 minutes. Cool to a temperature of 50°C and add a solution of skimmed milk powder reconstituted in  distilled/deionized water at a concentration (w/v) of 10% and sterilized by autoclaving at 121°C for 5 minutes.
2	CAPR	Cheese Agar Parmigiano Reggiano	Parmigiano Reggiano cheese grated 120.00 g/L, Sodium citrate 20.00 g/L, Agar 8.00 g/L. Dissolve the sodium citrate to distilled/deionized water and adjust the pH to 7.5. Add the Parmigiano Reggiano cheese to sodium citrate solution and gently heat in a thermostated bathroom set at 42°C for 50 minutes. Centrifuge the suspension at 8000 rpm, at 4°C  for 15 minutes . To separate the fat, filter the supernatant through gauze. Add the agar. pH 7.5 ± 0.2 at 25°C. Sterilize by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 minutes.
3	CAEM	Cheese Agar Emmental	Emmental cheese grated 120.00 g/L, Sodium citrate 20.00 g/L, Agar 8.00 g/L. Dissolve the sodium citrate to distilled/deionized water and adjust the pH to 7.5. Add the Parmigiano Reggiano cheese to sodium citrate solution and gently heat in a thermostated bathroom set at 42°C for 50 minutes. Centrifuge the suspension at 8000 rpm, at 4°C  for 15 minutes . To separate the fat, filter the supernatant through gauze. Add the agar. pH 7.5 ± 0.2 at 25°C. Sterilize by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 minutes.
4	CAM	Cheese Agar Milk	Parmigiano Reggiano cheese grated 120.00 g/L, Sodium citrate 20.00 g/L, Skimmed milk powder 7.00 g/L, Agar 8.00 g/L. Dissolve the sodium citrate to distilled/deionized water and adjust the pH to 7.5. Add the Parmigiano Reggiano cheese to sodium citrate solution and gently heat in a thermostated bathroom set at 42°C for 50 minutes. Centrifuge the suspension at 8000 rpm, at 4°C  for 15 minutes . To separate the fat, filter the supernatant through gauze. Add the agar. pH 7.5 ± 0.2 at 25°C. Sterilize by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 minutes. Cool to a temperature of 50°C and add a solution of skimmed milk powder reconstituted in distilled/deionized water at a concentration (w/v) of 10% and sterilized by autoclaving at 121°C for 5 minutes.
5	CAMY	Cheese Agar Milk Yeast	Parmigiano Reggiano cheese grated 120.00 g/L, Sodium citrate 20.00 g/L, Skimmed milk powder 7.00 g/L, Yeast extract 2.50 g/L, Agar 8.00 g/L. Dissolve the sodium citrate to distilled/deionized water and adjust the pH to 7.5. Add the Parmigiano Reggiano cheese to sodium citrate solution and gently heat in a thermostated bathroom set at 42°C for 50 minutes. Centrifuge the suspension at 8000 rpm, at 4°C  for 15 minutes . To separate the fat, filter the supernatant through gauze. Add yeast extract and agar. pH 7.5 ± 0.2 at 25°C. Sterilize by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 minutes. Cool to a temperature of 50°C and add a solution of skimmed milk powder reconstituted in distilled/deionized water at a concentration (w/v) of 10% and sterilized by autoclaving at 121°C for 5 minutes.
6	CAPT	Cheese Agar Pecorino Toscano	Pecorino Toscano cheese grated 120.00 g/L, Sodium citrate 20.00 g/L, Agar 8.00 g/L. Dissolve the sodium citrate to distilled/deionized water and adjust the pH to 7.5. Add the Pecorino Toscano cheese to sodium citrate solution and gently heat in a thermostated bathroom set at 42°C for 50 minutes. Centrifuge the suspension at 8000 rpm, at 4°C  for 15 minutes . To separate the fat, filter the supernatant through gauze. Add the agar. pH 7.5 ± 0.2 at 25°C. Sterilize by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 minutes.
